kings/theory/REVIEWS.md:323:6. **Two-sided shuttles — minor gap.** The §3 paragraph "With shuttles on both sides…" is labelled PROVED by Theorem 3.4, and §5.3 says the group "would be dud-type". Both rely on a two-sided version of Proposition 3.2 that is never proved. Two shuttles behave as dud only if each side's shuttle stays legal, and each side stays frozen, in all four combined king states.
